1
00:03:04,602 --> 00:03:08,936
Okay, okay. Here you go.

2
00:03:10,775 --> 00:03:12,185
And let's go again.

3
00:03:14,195 --> 00:03:15,776
Which one is this? Number nine?

4
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:17,319
Yeah, this is number nine.

5
00:03:17,573 --> 00:03:19,564
Bright Eyes, we call her.

6
00:03:20,534 --> 00:03:22,365
Are you watching this?

7
00:03:25,164 --> 00:03:26,370
This is unbelievable.

8
00:03:30,419 --> 00:03:32,125
Oh, my God.

9
00:03:33,214 --> 00:03:34,203
Oh, my God.

10
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:40,258
- How many moves was that?
- 20.

11
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:42,503
Yeah, a perfect score is 15.

12
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:43,928
Doc, what are you giving her?

13
00:03:44,225 --> 00:03:45,340
Hey, give me that video!

14
00:03:51,148 --> 00:03:53,685
Chimp number nine, just one dose.

15
00:03:53,776 --> 00:03:55,016
Aren't I seeing you later?

16
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,316
We are good to go.

17
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:58,735
I'm going to call you back.
Yeah, all right. Thanks. Bye.

18
00:03:58,823 --> 00:04:00,108
The 112. It works.

19
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:03,065
On just the one primate.

20
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:07,199
One is all we need.
Full cognitive recovery. We're ready.

21
00:04:07,832 --> 00:04:11,120
Look, are you sure you're not rushing this?

22
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:12,950
I've been working on this
for five and a half years.

23
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:15,373
The data is clear.

24
00:04:15,464 --> 00:04:16,829
We're ready, Steven.

25
00:04:16,924 --> 00:04:19,006
Look, are you sure you're not rushing this?

26
00:04:19,093 --> 00:04:20,754
For this, you're going to need
the board's approval.

27
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:23,714
There's a lot of money
riding on this, Will.

28
00:04:23,806 --> 00:04:25,046
You only get one shot.

29
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:27,051
One shot is all I need.

30
00:04:31,272 --> 00:04:32,682
All right. But I'll need to see

31
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:34,638
- all the research.
- You got it.

32
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,189
- And, Will...
- Yeah?

33
00:04:36,944 --> 00:04:39,060
Keep your personal emotions out of it.

34
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:41,896
These people invest in results, not dreams.

35
00:04:41,991 --> 00:04:43,106
Okay.

36
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:47,026
Meet chimp nine.

37
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:50,868
Here she is tasking at what is called
the Lucas Tower,

38
00:04:50,958 --> 00:04:54,450
the object of which is to move the tower
from peg to peg,

39
00:04:54,545 --> 00:04:58,288
without placing a larger block
on top of a smaller block.

40
00:04:58,382 --> 00:05:01,966
As expected, she was unable
to complete the puzzle at all.

41
00:05:02,052 --> 00:05:06,295
Then, we gave her what we call ALZ-112,

42
00:05:07,141 --> 00:05:11,100
a gene therapy that allows the brain
to create its own cells

43
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:12,767
in order to repair itself.

44
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:17,473
In biology, this is called neurogenesis.
Here at Gen-Sys,

45
00:05:19,028 --> 00:05:21,144
we call it the cure to Alzheimer's.

46
00:05:25,034 --> 00:05:26,524
Donnie, you get her ready?

47
00:05:26,619 --> 00:05:27,950
She's got stage fright.

48
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,405
Is that what it is?

49
00:05:35,044 --> 00:05:36,500
Hey! Hey!

50
00:05:40,341 --> 00:05:41,376
She is going to break my hand!

51
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:43,381
Let go. Bright Eyes, let go!

52
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:49,179
Are you all right?

53
00:05:56,482 --> 00:05:59,940
We're ready to move on to the next phase.
Human trials.

54
00:06:01,570 --> 00:06:05,028
Here you go, Bright Eyes.
It's your favorite fizzy soda, come on.

55
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:07,982
Let's go, Donnie.
We should have her downstairs already.

56
00:06:08,077 --> 00:06:10,238
Okay? Good girl.

57
00:06:12,206 --> 00:06:13,195
Come on out, girl. That's right.

58
00:06:15,376 --> 00:06:16,912
That's for you.

59
00:06:22,383 --> 00:06:23,623
Around the neck! Jesus!

60
00:06:26,387 --> 00:06:28,093
Donnie, do it now! Open up!

61
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:29,386
Donnie!

62
00:06:31,392 --> 00:06:32,381
I'm going to sedate her.

63
00:06:32,685 --> 00:06:35,427
- No, no, no, no!
- Door! Get the door! Bright Eyes!

64
00:06:38,399 --> 00:06:39,764
No, no, no, no.

65
00:06:41,443 --> 00:06:43,650
Close it down. Close it down now!

66
00:06:43,946 --> 00:06:45,561
Go get help. Donnie! Donnie! Come on.

67
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:49,027
There have been absolutely no side effects
associated with 112.

68
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:51,233
With one exception.

69
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:54,741
For some reason,
the chimps' irises exhibit flecks of green.

70
00:06:55,499 --> 00:06:57,706
Actually, we first noticed
it in chimp nine.

71
00:06:57,918 --> 00:07:01,581
Hence her nickname, Bright Eyes.
You will see when we bring her in.

72
00:07:07,219 --> 00:07:08,459
Watch out!

73
00:07:08,554 --> 00:07:09,839
In theory,

74
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:13,889
this therapy can be used to treat
a wide range of brain disorders.

75
00:07:19,773 --> 00:07:20,888
It is virtually limitless.

76
00:07:20,983 --> 00:07:24,567
As are the potential profits, which is why

77
00:07:24,653 --> 00:07:29,192
we are confident that
you will vote to approve human trials.

78
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,029
No! No!

79
00:07:56,435 --> 00:07:59,222
Mr. Jacobs? Mr. Jacobs, I am begging you.

80
00:07:59,313 --> 00:08:00,894
I am begging you not to do this.

81
00:08:00,981 --> 00:08:02,517
Look, it would cost a small fortune

82
00:08:02,608 --> 00:08:04,599
to run lab work-ups on all of those chimps

83
00:08:04,693 --> 00:08:06,149
only to tell me what I already know.

84
00:08:06,570 --> 00:08:08,276
That they are contaminated.

85
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:09,569
There are lives at stake here.

86
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:13,114
These are animals with personalities,
with attachments.

87
00:08:14,161 --> 00:08:15,901
- Attachments?
- Yeah.

88
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:19,154
I run a business, not a petting zoo.

89
00:08:20,042 --> 00:08:22,784
Find the most cost-effective way
to put those apes down.

90
00:08:22,878 --> 00:08:26,211
- I can't do that.
- You're the chimp handler. Handle it.

91
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:28,380
Steven?

92
00:08:29,218 --> 00:08:31,675
- Well, that was fun.
- They've taken the 112.

93
00:08:32,054 --> 00:08:33,419
The board have rejected your proposal.

94
00:08:33,514 --> 00:08:35,300
They've chosen to advance other programs.

95
00:08:35,516 --> 00:08:37,507
Well, there must be something
that you can do.

96
00:08:37,601 --> 00:08:39,808
Yes, there is. I could fire you.

97
00:08:39,895 --> 00:08:41,601
Believe me, we talked about it.

98
00:08:41,688 --> 00:08:44,020
We have five years of conclusive data.

99
00:08:44,108 --> 00:08:45,439
Parade all the data you want,

100
00:08:45,526 --> 00:08:48,563
you will never convince anyone
to invest another dime.

101
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:52,070
This drug has the potential to save lives.

102
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:53,693
To bankrupt this company, more like.

103
00:08:54,076 --> 00:08:57,489
I swear, you know everything
about the human brain

104
00:08:57,579 --> 00:08:59,035
except the way it works.

105
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:05,750
Go back to the drawing board on the 112.

106
00:09:05,838 --> 00:09:08,250
Start again in molecular development.

107
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:11,047
Find a way to get there
before someone else does.

108
00:09:12,970 --> 00:09:14,130
And clean up this mess.

109
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,236
Franklin?

110
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:43,246
They carry small.

111
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:46,496
She must have been pregnant
when they brought her in.

112
00:09:46,587 --> 00:09:47,793
So that's why...

113
00:09:49,089 --> 00:09:51,330
She wasn't being aggressive,
she was just being protective?

114
00:09:51,425 --> 00:09:52,915
She thought
we were going to hurt her baby.

115
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:55,417
Come here.

116
00:09:57,514 --> 00:10:00,631
I'd take him myself, but my brother-in-law
works for security.

117
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:02,632
He'd rat me out in a second.

118
00:10:04,479 --> 00:10:06,765
What, you want me to take it home?
I can't take care of a monkey.

119
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:10,019
- He's not a monkey, he's an ape.
- Franklin, I...

120
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:13,352
It's just for a couple days, until
I find a sanctuary. That's all I need.

121
00:10:13,447 --> 00:10:16,234
Franklin, no.
Look, this isn't my responsibility.

122
00:10:16,325 --> 00:10:18,111
This is company property.

123
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:24,488
Okay. I'm going to tell you what, Doc.

124
00:10:24,583 --> 00:10:27,199
Jacobs made me put down the other 12.

125
00:10:27,294 --> 00:10:28,579
I'm done.

126
00:10:31,548 --> 00:10:32,958
Be my guest.

127
00:10:57,157 --> 00:10:58,772
- Hey.
- Hi.

128
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:01,574
- Oh, you look beat.
- Yeah.

129
00:11:01,662 --> 00:11:03,277
How is he doing?

130
00:11:03,372 --> 00:11:05,988
Well, he has good days and bad days.

131
00:11:06,792 --> 00:11:10,580
Today, not so good. Although,
he has been quoting Shakespeare.

132
00:11:12,047 --> 00:11:13,412
Oh, you got a pet.

133
00:11:13,507 --> 00:11:15,668
Just a temporary house guest.

134
00:11:16,802 --> 00:11:17,837
Oh. Well, it might be good for him.

135
00:11:18,136 --> 00:11:19,922
- Yeah.
- Good night.

136
00:11:33,193 --> 00:11:34,433
Hey, Dad.

137
00:11:38,532 --> 00:11:40,363
- Dad?
- Will!

138
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:43,195
Hi. I don't hear you come in.

139
00:11:45,372 --> 00:11:47,112
Today is the day, right?

140
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:48,663
You thought I'd forget.

141
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:52,163
You have a big test today, right?
Chemistry?

142
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:58,127
Hey, Dad, do you want to see something?

143
00:11:58,427 --> 00:11:59,542
What?

144
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:11,345
What is that? Is he injured?

145
00:12:11,857 --> 00:12:14,189
No, I think that is a birthmark.

146
00:12:17,738 --> 00:12:19,444
"But as for Caesar,

147
00:12:20,157 --> 00:12:23,570
"kneel down, kneel down, and wonder."

148
00:12:23,744 --> 00:12:25,951
Yeah, don't get too attached.

149
00:12:27,289 --> 00:12:29,496
He is a cute little guy, isn't he?

150
00:13:16,963 --> 00:13:18,828
Where are my car keys?

151
00:13:21,176 --> 00:13:24,168
- My car keys! Where did you put them?
- Dad.

152
00:13:24,262 --> 00:13:26,628
You don't drive anymore.

153
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:30,181
I know that.

154
00:13:33,814 --> 00:13:35,020
Here,

155
00:13:36,775 --> 00:13:38,515
why don't you feed him?

156
00:13:38,610 --> 00:13:40,601
- Can you do that?
- Of course I can.

157
00:13:49,913 --> 00:13:51,778
Will, look at this.

158
00:13:55,669 --> 00:13:59,002
How old is he? A day old? Two days old?

159
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:01,086
Yeah.

160
00:14:01,925 --> 00:14:04,337
Well, he is a smart one, isn't he?

161
00:14:05,846 --> 00:14:08,132
What are you going to name him?

162
00:14:08,849 --> 00:14:10,339
I don't know.

163
00:14:21,445 --> 00:14:25,154
Right away, Caesar displayed
signs of heightened intelligence.

164
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:28,027
So I kept him and brought my work home.

165
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:40,243
By 18 months,

166
00:14:40,338 --> 00:14:44,081
Caesar was signing up to 24 words.

167
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:51,596
By age two,

168
00:14:51,683 --> 00:14:53,514
Caesar was completing puzzles and models

169
00:14:53,602 --> 00:14:56,389
designed for children eight years and up.

170
00:15:02,194 --> 00:15:03,684
At age three,

171
00:15:03,778 --> 00:15:05,985
Caesar continues to show cognitive skills

172
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:08,984
that far exceed
that of a human counterpart.

173
00:15:09,659 --> 00:15:12,196
Home. Home.

174
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:15,737
He completed the Lucas Tower
in fifteen moves,

175
00:15:15,832 --> 00:15:17,493
a perfect score.

176
00:15:17,918 --> 00:15:19,954
I maintain my hypothesis

177
00:15:20,045 --> 00:15:23,879
that, A, the green in his eyes
indicates that the ALZ-112

178
00:15:23,965 --> 00:15:26,923
was passed genetically from mother to son

179
00:15:27,052 --> 00:15:31,341
and, B, that in the absence
of damaged cells that need replacing,

180
00:15:31,431 --> 00:15:36,300
the drug in his system has radically
boosted healthy brain functioning.

181
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:41,055
And,

182
00:15:42,943 --> 00:15:44,774
he plays chess pretty well.

183
00:15:45,654 --> 00:15:47,940
It's my lamp! And my room!

184
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:51,110
Dad?

185
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:53,862
- I don't need you here.
- Irena, I'm sorry.

186
00:15:54,204 --> 00:15:55,569
I can't do this anymore.

187
00:15:55,664 --> 00:15:59,077
He belongs in a home.
This is no way for him to live.

188
00:16:02,712 --> 00:16:04,703
Yeah, and no way to live.

189
00:16:05,131 --> 00:16:07,122
No way to live.

190
00:16:09,636 --> 00:16:12,378
Now, it's my lamp. I'm always...

191
00:17:07,152 --> 00:17:09,359
It'll make you better, Dad.

192
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:25,457
Shh!

193
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:49,895
Dad?

194
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:52,064
Dad?

195
00:18:15,595 --> 00:18:17,927
Todd!
Come inside for breakfast!

196
00:18:37,158 --> 00:18:39,649
I'll need to keep track
of what I take from the lab.

197
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:42,326
Although, I don't foresee you needing
more than one treatment a month.

198
00:18:42,414 --> 00:18:43,904
- Something amazing has happened.
- Yeah.

199
00:18:43,998 --> 00:18:47,786
I'll need a blood test,
and a scan and the dosage.

200
00:18:47,919 --> 00:18:50,501
- You'll have to be carefully monitored.
- Will...

201
00:18:50,588 --> 00:18:51,748
Now if I can sneak some...

202
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,125
- Will!
- Yeah?

203
00:18:53,216 --> 00:18:54,296
I'm not sick anymore.

204
00:18:55,885 --> 00:18:57,546
It was nothing, Dad.

205
00:18:57,637 --> 00:19:00,003
Caesar. Where's Caesar? I want to see him.

206
00:19:07,856 --> 00:19:09,062
Caesar?

207
00:19:14,863 --> 00:19:16,023
Caesar!

208
00:19:16,114 --> 00:19:18,526
All right, he can't have gone far.

209
00:19:19,159 --> 00:19:20,365
Caesar!

210
00:19:21,703 --> 00:19:22,818
Daddy? Daddy!

211
00:19:22,996 --> 00:19:24,156
Caesar!

212
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:26,488
Get out of here! Get out!

213
00:19:29,043 --> 00:19:32,206
Get out! Get out of here!

214
00:19:32,797 --> 00:19:35,129
Hey, hey, hey! Enough! Enough!

215
00:19:36,134 --> 00:19:37,419
The hell is the matter with you?

216
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:39,751
If I see that animal anywhere
near my house or my kids again...

217
00:19:39,846 --> 00:19:41,006
He's not dangerous.

218
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:45,007
- It won't happen again.
- Damn right, it won't.

219
00:19:45,185 --> 00:19:46,675
Come on, Dad.

220
00:19:46,770 --> 00:19:48,510
He just wanted to play.

221
00:19:50,482 --> 00:19:52,188
Stay in the house.
Daddy's got it.

222
00:19:53,026 --> 00:19:55,517
I told you not to go out without us.

223
00:19:56,738 --> 00:19:58,478
Oh, God. It's okay.

224
00:20:00,283 --> 00:20:01,568
How bad is it?

225
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:03,524
I don't know.

226
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:25,380
He likes you.

227
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:26,889
Mmm-hmm.

228
00:20:26,976 --> 00:20:28,136
Don't worry.

229
00:20:28,228 --> 00:20:31,220
It'll be over soon
and we can go get a treat.

230
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:32,679
I'm thinking ice cream.

231
00:20:38,404 --> 00:20:39,439
Good idea.

232
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:42,401
You taught him to sign?

233
00:20:42,534 --> 00:20:44,820
Just a handful of things.

234
00:20:44,994 --> 00:20:46,404
Basic stuff.

235
00:20:48,373 --> 00:20:49,988
What's he saying?

236
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:51,118
Nothing.

237
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:54,162
So, when do you think
we should come back?

238
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:58,709
Well, you won't need to come back
because the stitches are dissolvable.

239
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:01,382
I would just say
watch out for signs of infection.

240
00:21:01,803 --> 00:21:03,134
Fever, redness.

241
00:21:06,057 --> 00:21:08,173
Okay. What's he saying now?

242
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:14,808
Well, he thinks that you and I
should have dinner together.

243
00:21:19,821 --> 00:21:21,027
I know.

244
00:21:24,868 --> 00:21:26,904
Hey, Caesar. Come on.

245
00:21:27,287 --> 00:21:29,278
Good to see you again, Caroline.

246
00:21:29,873 --> 00:21:31,613
You coming, Caesar?

247
00:21:31,958 --> 00:21:32,947
So, what's your secret?

248
00:21:34,919 --> 00:21:36,875
I can't take any credit. It's in his genes.

249
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:41,255
I think you're being very modest.
He's pretty amazing.

250
00:21:42,302 --> 00:21:45,886
I think you've built a pretty good home
for Caesar here.

251
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:47,299
But?

252
00:21:48,099 --> 00:21:50,431
He won't stay this way for long.

253
00:21:51,185 --> 00:21:54,177
He's gonna soon grow
into a large, powerful animal.

254
00:21:55,148 --> 00:21:56,228
Come here.

255
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:59,231
How has he been doing?

256
00:21:59,319 --> 00:22:00,809
Okay. I think.

257
00:22:02,655 --> 00:22:05,988
I love chimpanzees. I'm
also afraid of them.

258
00:22:07,452 --> 00:22:08,817
And it's appropriate to be afraid of them.

259
00:22:10,121 --> 00:22:11,406
Caesar would never hurt anyone.

260
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:13,496
Hey! Hey!

261
00:22:14,250 --> 00:22:16,115
He's happy here. Come on.

262
00:22:16,836 --> 00:22:17,996
Yeah, I can see that.

263
00:22:20,340 --> 00:22:22,171
Can we at least give him some open space?

264
00:22:22,258 --> 00:22:24,670
Yeah. That probably would be a good idea.

265
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:32,758
I know a place right across the bridge.
The redwoods. It's paradise.

266
00:22:48,618 --> 00:22:50,654
Come on. Come on.

267
00:22:51,955 --> 00:22:52,944
Come here.

268
00:22:53,039 --> 00:22:55,246
He doesn't need a leash.
He'll be fine. Come on.

269
00:22:55,541 --> 00:22:57,156
Just to be safe. Come on.

270
00:22:57,251 --> 00:22:59,037
Come on, Caesar.

271
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:04,963
This is the redwoods.

272
00:23:14,018 --> 00:23:16,555
Caesar? All right.

273
00:23:17,605 --> 00:23:21,018
If I take this off,
you cannot leave my sight.

274
00:23:21,567 --> 00:23:24,559
I would never find you again. Okay.

275
00:23:26,990 --> 00:23:29,322
- What is this?
- What's he doing?

276
00:23:29,867 --> 00:23:31,232
I don't believe that.

277
00:23:31,494 --> 00:23:34,327
- What?
- He's asking your permission.

278
00:23:34,914 --> 00:23:36,620
It's a supplicating gesture.

279
00:23:37,667 --> 00:23:38,998
It's okay.

280
00:23:41,087 --> 00:23:43,578
Come on, Caesar. Off you go!

281
00:23:54,976 --> 00:23:56,512
Look at him go.

282
00:23:57,478 --> 00:24:00,015
- Caesar!
- Caesar!

283
00:24:02,608 --> 00:24:04,473
- Caesar!
- Caesar!

284
00:24:06,946 --> 00:24:08,106
Caesar!

285
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:15,610
There you are.

286
00:24:16,998 --> 00:24:18,204
Caesar?

287
00:24:22,128 --> 00:24:23,959
Go on, Caesar. Climb!

288
00:24:28,509 --> 00:24:29,840
Go higher.

289
00:24:33,556 --> 00:24:34,716
Climb!

290
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:42,474
Just be careful.

291
00:24:44,859 --> 00:24:46,099
Caesar, be careful!

292
00:25:37,745 --> 00:25:39,030
Hi.

293
00:25:41,082 --> 00:25:42,993
What's going on, buddy?

294
00:25:43,668 --> 00:25:45,533
You get some love, too.

295
00:25:46,879 --> 00:25:48,369
Come on, honey.

296
00:25:49,132 --> 00:25:50,918
Is that a chimpanzee?

297
00:25:51,134 --> 00:25:52,214
Hi.

298
00:25:57,557 --> 00:25:58,592
Come on!

299
00:26:01,769 --> 00:26:03,009
Come on.

300
00:26:08,401 --> 00:26:10,608
Caesar? Caesar.

301
00:26:11,821 --> 00:26:13,061
Come on.

302
00:26:13,573 --> 00:26:15,734
It's all right. Come on.

303
00:26:19,245 --> 00:26:20,985
All right, come on.

304
00:26:25,251 --> 00:26:28,288
Let's go. You getting in?

305
00:26:30,965 --> 00:26:32,171
Caesar?

306
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:52,850
You okay, pal?

307
00:26:56,449 --> 00:26:58,189
Are you a pet? No.

308
00:26:59,994 --> 00:27:01,200
You're not a pet.

309
00:27:07,835 --> 00:27:08,950
I'm your father.

310
00:27:15,218 --> 00:27:16,754
What is Caesar?

311
00:27:19,931 --> 00:27:21,011
Okay.

312
00:27:28,481 --> 00:27:30,688
Caesar, this is where I work.

313
00:27:31,859 --> 00:27:33,815
This is where you were born.

314
00:27:34,528 --> 00:27:37,440
Your mother was here
with other chimpanzees.

315
00:27:40,993 --> 00:27:43,154
But she's not here anymore.

316
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:45,573
So,

317
00:27:47,083 --> 00:27:49,950
that's why I took you home to live with me.

318
00:27:57,343 --> 00:27:58,458
Yeah.

319
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:02,044
Your mother is dead.

320
00:28:04,892 --> 00:28:07,429
The thing is, she was given medicine.

321
00:28:08,854 --> 00:28:11,345
Like the medicine I give to Charles.

322
00:28:12,149 --> 00:28:14,105
She passed it on to you.

323
00:28:14,944 --> 00:28:16,400
That's why you're so smart.

324
00:28:19,991 --> 00:28:21,731
Let's take him home.

325
00:28:23,995 --> 00:28:25,075
Okay.

326
00:28:37,591 --> 00:28:40,048
Come on, explain it to me.

327
00:28:40,553 --> 00:28:42,043
All right.

328
00:28:43,055 --> 00:28:45,888
I snuck him out of the
lab to save his life.

329
00:28:45,975 --> 00:28:49,513
I had no idea that the effects had been
transferred vertically from his mother.

330
00:28:49,895 --> 00:28:53,683
But since then, he's been displaying
incredible signs of intelligence.

331
00:28:53,774 --> 00:28:57,858
I designed the 112 for repair,
but Caesar has gone way beyond that.

332
00:28:59,238 --> 00:29:01,194
Here is his IQ from last year.

333
00:29:01,282 --> 00:29:03,238
Since then, it's doubled.

334
00:29:05,786 --> 00:29:07,151
This is wrong, Will.

335
00:29:07,288 --> 00:29:10,496
My father was gone.
This drug brought him back.

336
00:29:10,583 --> 00:29:12,244
You never saw how bad he was.

337
00:29:12,668 --> 00:29:15,000
- He has his life again.
- And what about Caesar?

338
00:29:15,254 --> 00:29:17,870
- What about him?
- Where does he fit in?

339
00:29:18,924 --> 00:29:19,913
With me.

340
00:29:20,968 --> 00:29:22,048
With us.

341
00:29:22,762 --> 00:29:23,797
Listen,

342
00:29:24,555 --> 00:29:26,136
I know it's been hard for you,

343
00:29:26,974 --> 00:29:29,465
but you're trying to control things
that are not meant to be controlled.

344
00:29:29,810 --> 00:29:31,596
The 112 works.

345
00:29:32,146 --> 00:29:33,602
Do you realize how you sound?

346
00:29:33,689 --> 00:29:36,180
All I'm saying is,
this is a good thing.

347
00:29:36,275 --> 00:29:39,358
Caesar is proof of that. So is my father.

348
00:29:44,283 --> 00:29:45,272
Caesar, eat your food.

349
00:30:11,811 --> 00:30:13,472
Dad, are you okay?

350
00:30:14,313 --> 00:30:15,849
Yeah, I'm fine.

351
00:30:24,865 --> 00:30:26,230
Antibodies.

352
00:30:26,784 --> 00:30:29,742
His system has found a way
to fight the 112 virus

353
00:30:29,829 --> 00:30:31,945
so that it can't deliver its therapy.

354
00:30:32,998 --> 00:30:36,536
My father's disease
is going to return with a vengeance.

355
00:30:45,302 --> 00:30:47,634
Honey, have you seen the car wax?

356
00:30:47,721 --> 00:30:49,177
It's a Mustang.

357
00:30:55,855 --> 00:30:57,561
It's looking great. What did I do...

358
00:31:26,093 --> 00:31:27,333
Stop!

359
00:31:30,639 --> 00:31:31,845
You stop right now!

360
00:31:32,224 --> 00:31:33,509
Hey! Hey!

361
00:31:33,684 --> 00:31:36,471
Get out of there! Get out of that car!

362
00:31:36,896 --> 00:31:39,057
What the hell are you doing?
Get out of my car!

363
00:31:39,398 --> 00:31:42,515
I said get out of my car!

364
00:31:43,777 --> 00:31:45,813
I'm a pilot! I got to get to the airport!

365
00:31:45,905 --> 00:31:47,361
How am I going to get there now, huh?

366
00:31:48,073 --> 00:31:50,234
Answer the goddamned question!
What were you doing?

367
00:31:50,326 --> 00:31:51,486
I have a car just...

368
00:31:51,994 --> 00:31:53,029
Well, it's not obviously...

369
00:31:53,120 --> 00:31:54,735
That's it, I'm done.
The police can handle this.

370
00:31:55,915 --> 00:31:58,577
You stay right there!
You are going nowhere, mister!

371
00:31:58,667 --> 00:31:59,998
You or your son are going to pay for this!

372
00:32:00,085 --> 00:32:03,669
But I sure as hell am not going to!
This is your problem! You made the mess!

373
00:32:07,009 --> 00:32:08,419
- I'm sick of the two of you!
- I'm not going...

374
00:32:08,511 --> 00:32:10,092
You stay right there!

375
00:32:11,347 --> 00:32:12,587
No!

376
00:32:48,467 --> 00:32:49,752
No!

377
00:32:50,469 --> 00:32:52,005
No! No!

378
00:32:54,014 --> 00:32:55,470
Caesar! Stop!

379
00:32:57,268 --> 00:32:58,474
Daddy!

380
00:33:04,066 --> 00:33:05,431
No, no.

381
00:33:07,820 --> 00:33:08,980
Caesar!

382
00:33:19,957 --> 00:33:21,288
It's okay.

383
00:33:23,127 --> 00:33:25,334
It's okay. You didn't mean it.

384
00:33:26,839 --> 00:33:28,204
It's okay.

385
00:33:51,739 --> 00:33:54,401
Hey. Take that thing off of him.

386
00:33:55,743 --> 00:33:58,029
Will you take that thing off of him?
Come on.

387
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:59,906
Look. I'll take him in. Okay?

388
00:33:59,997 --> 00:34:02,079
No, he's under court orders.
You can't do that.

389
00:34:02,166 --> 00:34:03,656
It's fine, let him.

390
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:05,949
Bring him in when you're ready.

391
00:34:06,253 --> 00:34:08,619
- Take it off.
- Thank you.

392
00:34:09,923 --> 00:34:12,164
Caesar, Caesar, Caesar, Caesar? Caesar.

393
00:34:13,927 --> 00:34:16,043
Not right now. It's gonna be okay.

394
00:34:16,472 --> 00:34:18,303
Let's just see what it's like inside. Okay?

395
00:34:20,351 --> 00:34:22,387
Come on, Caesar. Let's go.

396
00:34:26,482 --> 00:34:28,814
Come on. Trust me.

397
00:34:44,583 --> 00:34:45,914
It's okay.

398
00:34:48,921 --> 00:34:49,910
Go on.

399
00:34:57,805 --> 00:35:00,763
He hasn't spent any time
with other chimps.

400
00:35:01,433 --> 00:35:02,764
We're used to that.

401
00:35:03,060 --> 00:35:06,097
He'll be a little skittish at first,
but we'll integrate him.

402
00:35:09,983 --> 00:35:11,974
You'd be surprised how quick they adapt.

403
00:35:12,945 --> 00:35:15,106
We provide a stimulating environment.

404
00:35:15,906 --> 00:35:17,942
He's going to thrive here.

405
00:35:18,283 --> 00:35:19,989
Come on, let's do some paperwork.

406
00:35:20,077 --> 00:35:23,285
Oh, and make sure you lock that door
when you come in.

407
00:35:46,937 --> 00:35:48,143
Caesar.

408
00:35:49,148 --> 00:35:51,059
It's gonna be okay.

409
00:35:52,276 --> 00:35:53,857
Everything is gonna be okay.

410
00:35:55,612 --> 00:35:57,022
Don't be scared.

411
00:35:57,114 --> 00:35:59,321
You're gonna stay here now.

412
00:36:02,161 --> 00:36:03,241
No.

413
00:36:04,496 --> 00:36:06,236
We're not going home right now.

414
00:36:06,331 --> 00:36:07,662
It's okay.

415
00:36:08,459 --> 00:36:11,747
In our experience,
the longer you drag out the goodbyes,

416
00:36:11,837 --> 00:36:13,793
the harder it is.

417
00:36:14,089 --> 00:36:16,171
Can I just sign that later?

418
00:36:17,760 --> 00:36:20,797
You'll probably miss him
more than he'll miss you.

419
00:36:20,888 --> 00:36:22,844
Best give him a couple of weeks
to get used to the place.

420
00:36:22,931 --> 00:36:24,671
Will, we have to go.

421
00:36:26,101 --> 00:36:27,762
We have to go home.

422
00:36:27,853 --> 00:36:29,844
I'm coming back soon. Okay?

423
00:36:35,944 --> 00:36:38,185
Just call ahead before you do.

424
00:36:42,367 --> 00:36:43,903
Hey, over here!

425
00:36:45,913 --> 00:36:47,824
Hey, I can get you out!

426
00:36:51,543 --> 00:36:53,875
Come on. Over here.

427
00:37:07,601 --> 00:37:09,637
Come on. Hey. Down here.

428
00:37:22,866 --> 00:37:24,356
Stupid monkey.

429
00:37:45,973 --> 00:37:49,807
Is that all you got? Come on!
It's a madhouse!

430
00:37:49,893 --> 00:37:51,804
It's a madhouse!

431
00:37:58,610 --> 00:38:01,192
Court order hasn't been filed,
so it's not in the system.

432
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:03,111
Once it comes through,
it'll take about 90 days

433
00:38:03,198 --> 00:38:04,438
before you receive an appeal date.

434
00:38:04,616 --> 00:38:06,356
- 90 days?
- Yes, sir, 90 days.

435
00:38:06,451 --> 00:38:08,442
- You'll be notified by mail.
- Hang on.

436
00:38:09,329 --> 00:38:11,945
Right. Here's what's gonna happen.
You're going to go back on your computer,

437
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,746
you're gonna shift things around,

438
00:38:13,834 --> 00:38:16,496
and you're going to get me a date
for my appeal this week. You got it?

439
00:38:17,087 --> 00:38:18,293
I can't help you.

440
00:38:18,797 --> 00:38:21,334
All right, then we have a problem.
Because I'm not moving until you do.

441
00:38:22,467 --> 00:38:23,957
90 days, sir.

442
00:38:24,052 --> 00:38:26,543
Be thankful
you're talking about court dates.

443
00:38:26,638 --> 00:38:28,799
You're lucky
they didn't put that animal down.

444
00:38:31,643 --> 00:38:34,180
I promise to get him back soon, Dad.

445
00:38:36,648 --> 00:38:37,683
Dad?

446
00:38:44,197 --> 00:38:47,985
My father's immune system
continues to reject the 112 virus,

447
00:38:48,076 --> 00:38:50,613
rendering the gene therapy obsolete.

448
00:38:50,996 --> 00:38:55,990
His health is deteriorating,
and the disease is progressing rapidly.

449
00:38:57,502 --> 00:38:59,584
I need a more aggressive virus strain.

450
00:38:59,671 --> 00:39:01,662
A faster delivery method.

451
00:39:02,841 --> 00:39:04,547
Because at this rate...

452
00:39:13,226 --> 00:39:14,386
I can't lose them both.

453
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:21,848
I won't lose them both.

454
00:39:24,863 --> 00:39:26,399
Hi. Can we talk?

455
00:39:26,615 --> 00:39:29,027
Make it fast. I've got a meeting.

456
00:39:30,369 --> 00:39:31,984
In the 10 years
you've been running Gen-Sys,

457
00:39:32,788 --> 00:39:34,324
how many drugs
have come down the pipeline

458
00:39:34,414 --> 00:39:36,370
that could save millions of lives,

459
00:39:36,708 --> 00:39:38,869
that could change everything?

460
00:39:38,961 --> 00:39:40,747
What are you talking about?

461
00:39:40,837 --> 00:39:42,543
The ALZ-112.

462
00:39:44,383 --> 00:39:46,590
What happened to you, Will?

463
00:39:46,677 --> 00:39:48,713
You used to be the star of this lab.

464
00:39:48,804 --> 00:39:50,965
Now you hardly ever show,
and when you do,

465
00:39:51,056 --> 00:39:54,640
you waste your time and that
of your team's fixating on a drug that,

466
00:39:54,726 --> 00:39:57,342
after what happened, is never,
ever going to get approved.

467
00:39:57,729 --> 00:40:00,766
The 112 is dangerous, Will,
and it doesn't work.

468
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:03,891
I treated my father with it. It does work.

469
00:40:06,863 --> 00:40:09,149
You did what? You did what?

470
00:40:09,241 --> 00:40:11,402
He beat the disease.
Like we predicted.

471
00:40:11,493 --> 00:40:13,825
- Bring him in.
- There's been a complication.

472
00:40:13,912 --> 00:40:15,197
Well, does it work, or doesn't it?

473
00:40:15,414 --> 00:40:17,780
My father's disease
eventually outran the cure.

474
00:40:17,874 --> 00:40:19,284
For goodness sake.

475
00:40:19,376 --> 00:40:22,960
His immune system produced antibodies
that beat the viral component,

476
00:40:23,088 --> 00:40:24,248
but it will work.

477
00:40:24,339 --> 00:40:28,673
I've already developed a virus strain
that I think will be more aggressive.

478
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:30,250
You think?

479
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:32,085
Just let me test it.

480
00:40:33,056 --> 00:40:34,921
You're wasting my time.

481
00:40:35,308 --> 00:40:36,548
There's more.

482
00:40:38,520 --> 00:40:41,353
The applications go beyond the disease.

483
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:42,555
There are indications that show

484
00:40:42,649 --> 00:40:46,517
that therapy can improve
cognitive functioning, memory quality...

485
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:48,818
What are you saying?

486
00:40:49,531 --> 00:40:52,989
My father didn't just recover. He improved.

487
00:40:54,036 --> 00:40:55,321
You mean increased intelligence?

488
00:40:56,204 --> 00:40:57,740
It's not conclusive, but yes.

489
00:40:59,875 --> 00:41:05,211
I want you to start testing
the revised 112 on chimps ASAP.

490
00:41:05,297 --> 00:41:07,754
- Okay.
- I'll give you whatever you need.

491
00:41:07,841 --> 00:41:09,206
Absolutely.

492
00:41:13,305 --> 00:41:14,841
Dinner time!

493
00:41:25,358 --> 00:41:26,768
Mmm.

494
00:41:26,860 --> 00:41:28,646
Grade A primate chow.

495
00:41:30,864 --> 00:41:32,070
Go on.

496
00:41:32,532 --> 00:41:34,443
Don't you know food when you see it?

497
00:41:46,421 --> 00:41:47,410
You think that's funny, huh?

498
00:41:50,175 --> 00:41:52,040
I'll show you something funny.

499
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:07,476
He'll learn who's boss soon enough.

500
00:42:09,778 --> 00:42:11,939
- What about his clothes?
- What about them?

501
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:13,019
I don't know.

502
00:42:13,782 --> 00:42:16,694
It might cause problems
with the other apes.

503
00:42:17,744 --> 00:42:19,700
Good.

504
00:43:22,934 --> 00:43:24,674
I've counted to 10 apes. Correct?

505
00:43:24,769 --> 00:43:25,929
Yep.

506
00:43:26,188 --> 00:43:27,428
Good. All the way to the back.

507
00:43:27,522 --> 00:43:28,602
Okay.

508
00:43:31,109 --> 00:43:34,101
You guys are moving really quick on this.
What's the big rush?

509
00:43:34,196 --> 00:43:36,061
First day back,
and you're still complaining.

510
00:43:52,130 --> 00:43:54,291
Koba. Hi, I'm Will.

511
00:44:04,351 --> 00:44:05,932
Okay. This one.

512
00:44:06,519 --> 00:44:08,760
He's very calm.

513
00:44:08,855 --> 00:44:10,846
Yeah, this guy has seen the inside
of a whole lot of labs.

514
00:44:10,941 --> 00:44:12,647
He knows the drill.

515
00:44:14,236 --> 00:44:15,567
Thought I'd join you.

516
00:44:15,737 --> 00:44:17,477
Watch our progress.

517
00:44:18,323 --> 00:44:19,984
Get him prepped.

518
00:44:24,871 --> 00:44:26,407
Tighten your masks.

519
00:44:26,498 --> 00:44:28,329
Pass me the 113.

520
00:44:29,459 --> 00:44:31,666
Pulse-ox is good,
blood pressure steady.

521
00:44:37,092 --> 00:44:39,128
Aerosol delivery in place.

522
00:44:44,516 --> 00:44:46,006
Releasing the 113.

523
00:45:05,203 --> 00:45:06,613
Franklin, get your mask on!

524
00:45:09,666 --> 00:45:11,327
- Got it?
- Yeah.

525
00:45:11,668 --> 00:45:12,783
Tighten the straps.

526
00:45:12,877 --> 00:45:14,083
You okay?

527
00:45:14,546 --> 00:45:15,877
Yeah, okay.

528
00:45:22,554 --> 00:45:24,215
Move it! Let's go!

529
00:45:25,015 --> 00:45:27,631
Get up and exercise, you lazy baboons!

530
00:48:11,222 --> 00:48:14,510
Intelligence results are remarkable.
No adverse effects.

531
00:48:14,601 --> 00:48:16,683
Apes have amazingly strong
immune systems.

532
00:48:16,769 --> 00:48:19,431
Yeah. All right, keep an eye on it.

533
00:48:19,522 --> 00:48:20,728
Okay.

534
00:48:21,858 --> 00:48:23,018
Sorry about that.

535
00:48:23,651 --> 00:48:26,393
These guys are more resilient than I am.

536
00:48:29,449 --> 00:48:31,030
Excuse me a sec.

537
00:49:02,315 --> 00:49:05,398
Hurt bad?

538
00:49:07,320 --> 00:49:10,357
You know sign?

539
00:49:11,449 --> 00:49:14,065
Circus Orangutan.

540
00:49:25,255 --> 00:49:26,586
He's good.

541
00:49:29,133 --> 00:49:33,467
Careful. Human no like smart Ape.

542
00:49:40,770 --> 00:49:42,886
I want you working late tonight.

543
00:49:42,981 --> 00:49:45,222
Gen-Sys needs three more of them.

544
00:50:06,045 --> 00:50:08,502
Hey. Hey. Hey!

545
00:50:10,842 --> 00:50:13,834
- Hey.
- Hey, Caesar. Hi.

546
00:50:13,928 --> 00:50:15,384
Are you hurt?

547
00:50:16,681 --> 00:50:18,171
Are you hurt?

548
00:50:18,558 --> 00:50:19,798
Show me.

549
00:50:23,354 --> 00:50:25,345
Caesar. Give me your hand.

550
00:50:25,690 --> 00:50:27,100
Give me your hand. It's okay.

551
00:50:27,191 --> 00:50:29,307
Sometimes the new kid on the block
gets picked on.

552
00:50:29,402 --> 00:50:32,189
Don't worry.
God, what have they done to you?

553
00:50:33,281 --> 00:50:35,272
That's bullshit. What the hell did you do?

554
00:50:35,366 --> 00:50:38,278
- Let go, man.
- Hey! What's the problem here?

555
00:50:40,413 --> 00:50:42,324
I'm taking him out of here. Right now.

556
00:50:42,415 --> 00:50:44,952
Not without a court order, you're not.

557
00:50:45,043 --> 00:50:46,783
He's not yours anymore.

558
00:50:46,878 --> 00:50:50,245
I promise, if I find out
he's been mistreated in any way,

559
00:50:50,340 --> 00:50:52,331
I'll have this place shut down.

560
00:50:54,302 --> 00:50:55,462
Go on.

561
00:50:56,095 --> 00:50:57,881
Hey. Hi.

562
00:50:59,932 --> 00:51:01,047
Hey.

563
00:51:04,062 --> 00:51:05,051
No.

564
00:51:06,230 --> 00:51:07,561
No, we're not going home right now.

565
00:51:09,901 --> 00:51:12,233
But I'm going to get you out of here.
I promise.

566
00:51:15,073 --> 00:51:16,062
You have to trust me.

567
00:51:16,908 --> 00:51:19,149
Caesar, you have to trust me. Okay?

568
00:51:19,243 --> 00:51:21,325
I think this visit is over.

569
00:51:21,704 --> 00:51:24,366
Trust me. It'll be okay.

570
00:52:08,334 --> 00:52:10,620
Come on! Move it! Let's go!

571
00:52:57,884 --> 00:52:59,590
Wow! There's hundreds of them.

572
00:52:59,677 --> 00:53:01,417
This is like your own private zoo.

573
00:53:01,512 --> 00:53:02,843
More like a prison for hairy dudes.

574
00:53:04,182 --> 00:53:05,672
They watch TV?

575
00:53:05,892 --> 00:53:07,757
We call it enrichment.

576
00:53:10,229 --> 00:53:12,185
This one's so cute!

577
00:53:13,065 --> 00:53:14,680
What's his name?

578
00:53:16,110 --> 00:53:18,726
The name is Cornelia. It's a she.

579
00:53:20,364 --> 00:53:21,854
- Oh, my God!
- Don't get too close.

580
00:53:21,949 --> 00:53:23,610
This one scared me
half to death.

581
00:53:23,701 --> 00:53:25,817
Yeah. That big guy's called Maurice.

582
00:53:26,370 --> 00:53:27,576
No fun.

583
00:53:28,247 --> 00:53:30,704
Here, I'll show you something fun.

584
00:53:34,587 --> 00:53:36,123
Check this out.

585
00:53:39,300 --> 00:53:40,915
Are you insane?

586
00:53:42,261 --> 00:53:44,001
You shouldn't be in here.

587
00:53:44,096 --> 00:53:45,427
Hey, you're next!

588
00:53:52,230 --> 00:53:54,095
Come on, let's go.

589
00:53:54,190 --> 00:53:56,397
I spend too much time in here as it is.

590
00:53:58,486 --> 00:53:59,521
Come on.

591
00:53:59,612 --> 00:54:01,352
Check out this guy.

592
00:54:01,614 --> 00:54:03,320
Hey, that one is a pain in the ass.

593
00:54:03,407 --> 00:54:04,396
Thinks he's special or something.

594
00:54:06,744 --> 00:54:07,904
Freaky.

595
00:54:08,913 --> 00:54:10,369
Hey, come here.

596
00:54:11,707 --> 00:54:13,038
It's like he's thinking or something...

597
00:54:15,086 --> 00:54:16,997
Oh, my God! He's got his throat!

598
00:54:17,255 --> 00:54:18,461
- Let him go!
- Let go!

599
00:54:21,509 --> 00:54:23,500
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

600
00:54:24,470 --> 00:54:26,506
I told you not to get too close, man.

601
00:54:26,597 --> 00:54:28,428
Come on, guys. Let's get out of here.

602
00:59:15,094 --> 00:59:16,174
Hey.

603
00:59:17,805 --> 00:59:20,512
Some things aren't meant to be changed.

604
00:59:21,225 --> 00:59:23,216
You need to accept that.

605
00:59:27,022 --> 00:59:28,603
Hey!

606
00:59:28,691 --> 00:59:31,558
Hey! What's going on here?

607
00:59:31,652 --> 00:59:33,142
More 113 trials. We're just prepping...

608
00:59:33,237 --> 00:59:35,899
No, we have to analyze
Koba's blood work first.

609
00:59:36,031 --> 00:59:37,066
Franklin knows this. Where is he?

610
00:59:37,616 --> 00:59:39,572
He's been out sick for two days.

611
00:59:39,660 --> 00:59:41,321
Well, I didn't authorize this.

612
00:59:41,412 --> 00:59:43,243
No.

613
00:59:43,330 --> 00:59:44,490
I did.

614
00:59:44,832 --> 00:59:46,993
We agreed to test sparingly on one subject.

615
00:59:47,084 --> 00:59:49,496
And that one subject is stunning.

616
00:59:49,879 --> 00:59:52,712
It's a virus,
we don't know the human-related effects.

617
00:59:52,798 --> 00:59:56,040
The drug works, Will. Tell him, Linda.

618
00:59:56,135 --> 00:59:59,502
For starters, Koba scored a perfect 15
on the Lucas Tower.

619
00:59:59,597 --> 01:00:01,633
Every test result
verifies its effectiveness.

620
01:00:01,724 --> 01:00:03,260
- No more tests.
- What are you...

621
01:00:03,350 --> 01:00:05,511
Not until we have a better understanding
of what we're dealing with.

622
01:00:05,603 --> 01:00:08,561
Look, I'll tell you exactly what we're...
Look. Just give us a minute.

623
01:00:08,647 --> 01:00:11,059
Excuse me, put the ape back in the cage,
and be gentle.

624
01:00:11,150 --> 01:00:14,859
Will, I'll tell you exactly
what we're dealing with here.

625
01:00:14,945 --> 01:00:15,900
We're dealing with a drug

626
01:00:15,988 --> 01:00:20,072
that is worth more than everything
else we are developing combined.

627
01:00:20,576 --> 01:00:24,364
You make history, I make money.
Wasn't that our arrangement?

628
01:00:24,455 --> 01:00:25,865
No, there are risks.

629
01:00:25,956 --> 01:00:27,912
Don't talk to me about risks.

630
01:00:28,000 --> 01:00:31,413
You gave your own father
an experimental drug.

631
01:00:31,503 --> 01:00:33,789
I could finish your career
with one phone call.

632
01:00:33,881 --> 01:00:36,338
I'll save you the trouble. I quit.

633
01:00:37,468 --> 01:00:39,629
We will proceed without you.

634
01:00:41,639 --> 01:00:44,221
Look, you don't know what you're doing.

635
01:00:44,308 --> 01:00:45,764
These tests need to be contained.

636
01:00:45,851 --> 01:00:50,595
You have no idea if the 113 is stable,
what kind of damage it can do to people.

637
01:00:50,689 --> 01:00:53,681
Yes. Well, that is why
we test it on chimps.

638
01:00:54,818 --> 01:00:55,807
Isn't it?

639
01:00:57,529 --> 01:01:00,066
Dr. Rodman, it's me, Franklin!
I need to talk to you!

640
01:01:00,157 --> 01:01:02,148
Can you come to the door?

641
01:01:15,339 --> 01:01:16,579
Doc?

642
01:01:16,674 --> 01:01:18,539
Who the hell are you?

643
01:01:22,513 --> 01:01:24,049
Get out of here!

644
01:01:24,139 --> 01:01:25,925
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

645
01:01:42,199 --> 01:01:44,064
You wouldn't be trying to entrap me,
would you?

646
01:01:48,205 --> 01:01:51,197
Well, I can't say I approve.

647
01:01:52,751 --> 01:01:54,036
They're not people, you know.

648
01:01:54,461 --> 01:01:55,826
You gonna let him go or not?

649
01:02:09,601 --> 01:02:11,933
Caesar? Hey, come on.

650
01:02:13,439 --> 01:02:14,895
Come on, we're going home.

651
01:02:17,568 --> 01:02:18,683
Home.

652
01:02:19,862 --> 01:02:21,022
Come on, we're really going.

653
01:02:22,281 --> 01:02:24,897
Come on. Let's get out of here.

654
01:02:33,917 --> 01:02:34,997
Yeah.

655
01:02:36,086 --> 01:02:37,075
Come on.

656
01:02:45,637 --> 01:02:46,843
Caesar?

657
01:02:49,141 --> 01:02:52,349
I guess he likes it better here
with his own kind.

658
01:05:24,546 --> 01:05:27,879
Why cookie Rocket?

659
01:05:32,095 --> 01:05:34,677
Apes alone...

660
01:05:34,806 --> 01:05:37,718
weak.

661
01:05:39,061 --> 01:05:43,270
Apes together strong.

662
01:05:55,827 --> 01:05:58,569
Apes stupid.

663
01:06:08,298 --> 01:06:10,835
Damn it, Rodney!
You leave the hose out in the atrium again?

664
01:06:10,926 --> 01:06:12,166
What? No!

665
01:08:36,071 --> 01:08:37,936
Come on! Let's go!

666
01:08:42,786 --> 01:08:44,401
Come on, get up!

667
01:09:35,130 --> 01:09:38,588
Eight months after its launch, Earth's
first manned space flight to Mars...

668
01:09:38,675 --> 01:09:40,415
I swear, Dodge,
I'm telling the truth.

669
01:09:40,510 --> 01:09:42,501
Yeah, well, if you didn't take my cookies
then who the hell did?

670
01:09:42,596 --> 01:09:44,086
- I don't know.
- Hey!

671
01:09:44,264 --> 01:09:46,971
Will you two morons knock it off?

672
01:09:48,852 --> 01:09:50,342
I'm going home.

673
01:09:53,523 --> 01:09:56,014
I get more peace
in the goddamn ape house.

674
01:09:56,109 --> 01:09:57,645
Dad, I'm sorry.

675
01:09:59,237 --> 01:10:01,478
- Well done, Rodney.
- I swear...

676
01:10:55,752 --> 01:10:57,788
Mr. Franklin? It's Dottie.

677
01:11:04,302 --> 01:11:05,792
Mr. Franklin?

678
01:11:06,805 --> 01:11:07,840
Hello?

679
01:11:30,787 --> 01:11:32,277
What the hell?

680
01:11:35,083 --> 01:11:39,952
God said, "Let the waters
bring forth moving creatures..."

681
01:11:40,213 --> 01:11:42,454
Rodney, get to the platform now.

682
01:11:47,721 --> 01:11:48,927
Rodney!

683
01:12:00,859 --> 01:12:02,975
What the hell do you think
you're doing, huh?

684
01:12:17,751 --> 01:12:18,866
Get!

685
01:12:22,672 --> 01:12:25,334
Go on. Get back in your cage.

686
01:12:26,426 --> 01:12:28,166
I'm warning you.

687
01:12:31,973 --> 01:12:33,509
Go on, get!

688
01:12:37,228 --> 01:12:38,343
That's it.

689
01:12:39,773 --> 01:12:42,480
See? That's what you get! Now get back!

690
01:12:43,985 --> 01:12:45,020
What's wrong with you?

691
01:12:47,030 --> 01:12:48,611
Dumb monkey!

692
01:12:59,751 --> 01:13:03,039
Take your stinking paw off me,
you damn dirty ape!

693
01:13:06,424 --> 01:13:07,630
No!

694
01:13:20,814 --> 01:13:21,849
No!

695
01:13:27,278 --> 01:13:31,612
No! No! No!

696
01:13:32,409 --> 01:13:34,570
No! No!

697
01:13:34,828 --> 01:13:36,068
No!

698
01:14:23,126 --> 01:14:24,286
No!

699
01:14:47,817 --> 01:14:49,682
I swear I'm gonna skin
each and every one of you!

700
01:15:51,005 --> 01:15:52,961
Caroline, have you been up
to Caesar's room?

701
01:15:58,805 --> 01:16:00,215
No one is answering.

702
01:16:32,130 --> 01:16:33,415
Landon?

703
01:17:03,953 --> 01:17:05,113
Will?

704
01:17:07,582 --> 01:17:08,697
Will!

705
01:17:13,755 --> 01:17:15,245
What happened?

706
01:17:15,882 --> 01:17:16,871
He spoke.

707
01:17:19,302 --> 01:17:20,792
What do you... What?

708
01:17:21,387 --> 01:17:22,627
Your ape.

709
01:17:23,890 --> 01:17:25,346
He spoke.

710
01:18:12,230 --> 01:18:13,891
What in the hell?

711
01:18:15,191 --> 01:18:16,601
I don't believe this.

712
01:18:16,693 --> 01:18:19,230
...I'm gonna skin
each and every one of you!

713
01:18:22,740 --> 01:18:25,652
I need someone to coordinate
with the SFPD. Tell them we got a fatality.

714
01:18:25,910 --> 01:18:28,526
- What is it?
- I know where he's headed.

715
01:18:38,589 --> 01:18:39,829
Len?

716
01:18:41,384 --> 01:18:42,624
Let's go.

717
01:19:10,246 --> 01:19:13,579
- Jacobs.
- Mr. Jacobs, it's Linda from Will's team.

718
01:19:13,666 --> 01:19:15,497
Something horrible has happened.

719
01:19:15,585 --> 01:19:18,292
Franklin is dead, from a viral infection.

720
01:19:18,379 --> 01:19:19,994
The hell are you talking about?

721
01:19:20,089 --> 01:19:22,000
He was exposed to the 113.

722
01:19:22,091 --> 01:19:24,207
It does something to people
that it doesn't do to apes.

723
01:19:26,429 --> 01:19:28,920
He'll have to go through the city
and across the bridge.

724
01:19:29,265 --> 01:19:32,007
Mr. Jacobs? Mr. Jacobs, are you...

725
01:19:32,101 --> 01:19:33,090
What the hell?

726
01:20:05,551 --> 01:20:07,041
Steven Jacobs!

727
01:20:07,470 --> 01:20:09,006
This is my facility. We've had a breach.

728
01:20:09,138 --> 01:20:10,423
We need to get up in the air

729
01:20:10,515 --> 01:20:12,722
and track them down
and destroy them! Okay?

730
01:20:12,809 --> 01:20:14,094
Wait a sec! Wait a second.

731
01:20:14,185 --> 01:20:17,097
Look. You've got to trust me on this! Okay?

732
01:20:36,666 --> 01:20:38,281
You guys might want
to get your cameras ready.

733
01:20:38,376 --> 01:20:40,913
Normally these guys are quite shy.

734
01:21:07,363 --> 01:21:09,354
They just tore through a park
on the north side.

735
01:21:09,699 --> 01:21:12,281
- They're being led!
- Got to hold the button!

736
01:21:12,368 --> 01:21:13,858
- What?
- The button!

737
01:21:13,953 --> 01:21:16,695
They're being led!
These apes are smarter than you think!

738
01:21:16,789 --> 01:21:18,199
We've got to kill the leader!

739
01:23:11,654 --> 01:23:13,940
No, you do not tell them
I am stuck in traffic.

740
01:23:14,031 --> 01:23:16,693
You make up something smarter! Hold on.

741
01:23:18,661 --> 01:23:20,117
What the...

742
01:23:35,261 --> 01:23:36,250
They're on the bridge.

743
01:23:36,887 --> 01:23:38,627
They're trying to get to the redwoods.

744
01:23:41,642 --> 01:23:44,759
SFPD Police One, this is Air Ops.

745
01:23:44,854 --> 01:23:48,346
Seal off the south end.
What's the status of the mounted units?

746
01:23:48,441 --> 01:23:49,521
Good to go, sir.

747
01:23:49,650 --> 01:23:52,266
All right.
As soon as they reach you, push north!

748
01:24:01,537 --> 01:24:03,903
North side,
we're going to push them right to you.

749
01:24:03,998 --> 01:24:05,363
No problem,
we're ready for them.

750
01:24:05,541 --> 01:24:06,781
North side is locked.

751
01:24:06,876 --> 01:24:09,288
They'll never get through here.

752
01:24:20,890 --> 01:24:23,222
As soon as they hit the gap,
we'll take them out!

753
01:24:23,309 --> 01:24:26,016
- You're going to shoot them?
- Like shooting fish in a barrel.

754
01:24:26,979 --> 01:24:28,059
Good.

755
01:24:32,151 --> 01:24:34,984
Turn that thing around. Keep moving.
Get off this bridge, sir.

756
01:24:35,071 --> 01:24:36,811
- No, you don't understand.
- You don't understand!

757
01:24:36,906 --> 01:24:39,739
Get off this bridge now!
This is an evacuation. Get out!

758
01:24:39,825 --> 01:24:41,690
- All civilians clear.
- Please confirm.

759
01:24:41,786 --> 01:24:43,492
Get these people off the bridge!

760
01:24:49,210 --> 01:24:50,575
Wait!

761
01:25:03,599 --> 01:25:04,634
Go up.

762
01:25:14,151 --> 01:25:15,516
Get under.

763
01:25:30,209 --> 01:25:31,745
Stand by to send in mounted units.

764
01:25:34,630 --> 01:25:35,619
They're gonna slaughter them.

765
01:25:38,592 --> 01:25:41,129
- I'm going to get Caesar.
- Hey. Hey, hey.

766
01:25:41,220 --> 01:25:42,426
Listen.

767
01:25:44,807 --> 01:25:46,513
You be careful.

768
01:25:47,643 --> 01:25:48,849
Hey!

769
01:25:50,104 --> 01:25:51,640
Get down from there.
You're not allowed up there.

770
01:25:51,731 --> 01:25:53,847
But I have to get to my car! Let go of me!

771
01:25:53,983 --> 01:25:55,519
I've got to get to my car. It's important!

772
01:25:55,609 --> 01:25:56,644
Hey!

773
01:25:59,280 --> 01:26:00,861
Push them north!

774
01:26:06,620 --> 01:26:08,531
Get out of the way!

775
01:26:51,123 --> 01:26:52,238
No!

776
01:27:09,850 --> 01:27:11,715
Quick or you'll lose them
in the fog!

777
01:27:12,061 --> 01:27:13,050
Do it!

778
01:27:28,244 --> 01:27:30,326
Where are they? I can't see them.

779
01:27:35,000 --> 01:27:37,161
CHP North, do you have a visual?

780
01:27:37,253 --> 01:27:38,413
No, sir. Negative.

781
01:28:06,448 --> 01:28:07,858
Safeties off!

782
01:28:28,470 --> 01:28:31,212
Hold your fire! Hold your fire!

783
01:29:18,145 --> 01:29:20,932
Get back! Get back!
Everybody, pull back!

784
01:29:42,753 --> 01:29:44,084
Caesar!

785
01:30:04,233 --> 01:30:05,894
That's him. That's the leader.

786
01:30:12,741 --> 01:30:15,357
255, come in! Are you there?

787
01:31:45,626 --> 01:31:47,207
Help me.

788
01:31:48,837 --> 01:31:50,327
Help me.

789
01:32:05,979 --> 01:32:07,139
Take my hand.

790
01:32:07,898 --> 01:32:09,229
Come on. Come on.

791
01:32:12,361 --> 01:32:13,396
Come on.

792
01:32:16,657 --> 01:32:17,942
Come on.

793
01:32:19,618 --> 01:32:20,653
No.

794
01:32:27,126 --> 01:32:28,366
Come on.

795
01:32:30,379 --> 01:32:31,619
Not you.

796
01:32:33,340 --> 01:32:34,705
No! No!

797
01:32:39,680 --> 01:32:41,216
Stupid monkey!

798
01:32:41,390 --> 01:32:43,631
No! No!

799
01:33:43,952 --> 01:33:45,158
Caesar!

800
01:33:52,294 --> 01:33:53,283
Caesar?

801
01:34:33,502 --> 01:34:34,582
Caesar.

802
01:34:36,338 --> 01:34:39,171
I'm sorry. This is my fault.

803
01:34:40,801 --> 01:34:43,668
This has to stop. This isn't the way.

804
01:34:44,596 --> 01:34:46,461
You know what they're capable of.

805
01:34:48,475 --> 01:34:49,840
Please come home.

806
01:34:51,103 --> 01:34:53,970
If you come home, I'll protect you.

807
01:35:13,917 --> 01:35:15,873
Caesar is home.

808
01:35:22,884 --> 01:35:24,124
Okay.

809
01:35:26,346 --> 01:35:27,552
Caesar is home.

810
01:35:30,851 --> 01:35:31,886
Go.

811
01:37:35,183 --> 01:37:37,640
An unknown group
have caused a major disturbance

812
01:37:37,727 --> 01:37:39,137
here in the Bay Area,

813
01:37:39,229 --> 01:37:42,062
including the City Zoo
and the Golden Gate Bridge,

814
01:37:42,149 --> 01:37:44,936
causing widespread damage
and some reported injuries.

815
01:37:45,444 --> 01:37:49,687
Eyewitnesses have also reported
seeing apes running through the city.

